     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am building an application with an input box and submitting buttons <div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div>fluidRow(</div><div>          box(title = &quot;Fold Change Analysis&quot;,solidHeader = T,status = &quot;primary&quot;,width=8,</div><div>            textInput(&quot;FCThreshold&quot;, label = h3(&quot;Fold Change Threshold:&quot;)),</div><div>            actionButton(&quot;FCSubmit&quot;, label=&quot;Submit&quot;),</div><div>            actionButton(&quot;FCReset&quot;, label=&quot;Reset&quot;)  </div><div>          )</div><div>          </div><div>        )</div></div></code></div><br>But the two buttons lies in the left of the box. How can I put them in the middle of the box? I heard that css may be suitable for solving this problem, but I am not familiar with css. I appreciate it if you can give me a solution in detail.</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-tkE6uz06qxI/Vio4pXTmBbI/AAAAAAAAACU/fC2JGXOaDEA/s1600/QQ%25E6%2588%25AA%25E5%259B%25BE20151023213902.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-tkE6uz06qxI/Vio4pXTmBbI/AAAAAAAAACU/fC2JGXOaDEA/s1600/QQ%2525E6%252588%2525AA%2525E5%25259B%2525BE20151023213902.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396307991000&amp;usg=AOvVaw09i4AX7ilf3m5nJ8UcX8SB\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-tkE6uz06qxI/Vio4pXTmBbI/AAAAAAAAACU/fC2JGXOaDEA/s320/QQ%25E6%2588%25AA%25E5%259B%25BE20151023213902.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"148\"></a><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-tkE6uz06qxI/Vio4pXTmBbI/AAAAAAAAACU/fC2JGXOaDEA/s1600/QQ%25E6%2588%25AA%25E5%259B%25BE20151023213902.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\